```js
// Initialize the React‑state manager with your own config, store, context and hooks
const { store, context, hooks } = manageReactState(
  {
    initialState: initialStateObject,          // <-- your initial state
    reducers: reducersMap,                    // <-- your reducer map
    middlewares: [loggerMiddleware],          // <-- logger middleware
    enhancers: [applyMiddleware('myMiddleWare')] // <-- enhancer that applies your middleware
  },
  store,      // <-- the store instance (or its name if you prefer a string)
  context,    // <-- the React context object
  { useStateSelectorHook, useDispatchActionHook } // <-- custom hooks for components
);
```

This single line creates the store, provides the context, and wires up the custom hooks (`useStateSelectorHook` and `useDispatchActionHook`) so that your components can read from and dispatch actions to the shared state.

